          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A park ranger at a remote station receives a locator beacon from a lost hiker. The signal indicates the hiker is at a bearing of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "070^\\circ",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " from the station. The ranger hikes 7 km along this bearing.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p31-q21-second-beacon",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Upon arrival, a second beacon is received: from the ranger’s new position, the hiker is now at a bearing of ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "150^\\circ",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The ranger then walks a further 5 km in that direction and locates the hiker.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p31-q21-request",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What are the distance and bearing of the hiker’s final position relative to the ranger station? Give the distance correct to two decimal places and the bearing correct to the nearest degree.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p31-q21-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "9.28 km at bearing ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "102^\\circ",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p31-q21-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use the included angle ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "100^\\circ",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " to find the distance, then the angle form of the cosine rule to find the bearing.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $S$ be the station, $R$ the ranger’s position after 7 km and $H$ the hiker. The return bearing from $R$ to $S$ is $250^\\circ$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle SRH&=250^\\circ-150^\\circ\\\\\\angle SRH&=100^\\circ\\\\SH^2&=7^2+5^2-2(7)(5)\\cos100^\\circ\\\\SH&=\\sqrt{74-70\\cos100^\\circ}\\\\SH&\\approx9.2819918356\\text{ km}\\end{align*}$$\n\nLet $\\alpha=\\angle RSH$. Use the unrounded value of $SH$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac{7^2+SH^2-5^2}{2(7)(SH)}\\\\\\alpha&\\approx32.038822389^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe bearing of $H$ from $S$ is clockwise from the initial bearing:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Bearing}&=070^\\circ+\\alpha\\\\\\text{Bearing}&\\approx102.038822389^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe hiker is 9.28 km from the station at bearing $102^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
